    "lawCode": "Amd §461-b, Soc Serv L; amd §4653, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Social Services Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5540\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the social services law, in relation to licensed opera-\ntors of adult care facilities and their affiliates; and to amend the\npublic health law, in relation to licensed operators of assisted living\nfacilities and their affiliates\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would authorize affiliates of licensed operators in good\nstanding to utilize the streamlined application process for adult care\nfacilities and assisted living residences.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends Social Services Law section 461-b(2)(b) to authorize\naffiliates of licensed operators in good standing to utilize the stream-\nlined application process that the Department of Health has established\nfor licensure as an adult care facility.\n\nSection 2 makes a conforming amendment to Public Health Law section\n4653(2) to authorize affiliates of licensed operators in good standing\nto utilize the same streamlined application process for licensure as an\nassisted living residence.\n\nSection 3 provides for an immediate effective date.\n\nEXITING LAW:\n\nSocial Services Law section 461-b(2)(b) and Public Health Law section\n4653(2) directed the Department of Health to develop a new streamlined\nprocess for \"existing licensed operators in good standing\" seeking\napproval of an additional facility of the same type.In 2014, pursuant to\nthese statutes, the Department established this new streamlined applica-\ntion process (https://www.health.ny.gov/forms/doh-5105.pdf).\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nUnder the new streamlined application process, an existing licensed\noperator in good standing can receive Department approval to operate a\nnew facility of the same type in as fast as 60 days. This new stream-\nlined process is a substantial improvement over past practice, and holds\ngreat promise for the assisted living industry.\n\nHowever, one unforeseen technical problem that has arisen is that many\nassisted living companies utilize a different legal entity for each new\nfacility they open or acquire (typically for accounting or liability\npurposes). As the Department has identified, such a new legal entity\ncannot itself be considered a \"licensed operator in good standing\" and\ntherefore would not be able to avail itself of the new streamlined proc-\n\ness. To remedy this unforeseen problem, this bill would expressly\nauthorize \"affiliates\" of licensed operators in good standing to utilize\nthe streamlined process.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
